  "about": "Each test file as Simple Presenter's own editor reads it: what its chord editors are handed (PresentationEditor::song). One entry for each text box that has words of its own, in the order of the slides: `slide` counted from 0, the name of its group and whether it is the first slide of that group, the id of the text box, its words, and its chords, each `at` a place along those words (a line break being one). `key` is the key the chords are written in, as a musician writes it, or nothing. This is the reference for reading a file: a port that reads these files should find the same. Some strings hold characters that cannot be seen: U+200B and U+2001.",
  "madeBy": "tools/simple-presenter-scripts/dump.qml, run in Simple Presenter (testdata/README.md says how). Do not edit by hand.",
